<title>USA: Security Bancorp stake cut by group.</title>
<headline>Security Bancorp stake cut by group.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group including Eighteen Seventy Financial Inc said on Monday it cut its stake in Security Bancorp to 74,000 common shares or 4.984 percent from 7.07 percent previously held.</p>
<p>In a filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission, the company said its latest transactions include the sale of 71,000 common shares sold between Oct 9 and Oct 25 at prices ranging from $29 to $29.1875 per share.</p>
<p>The company said it holds the stake for investment purposes.</p>
<p>Eighteen Seventy is a wholly-owned subsidiary of Eighteen Seventy Corp.</p>
